    "instructions": [
        "Heat the olive oil in a large pot or Dutch oven. Add the onions and cook over medium-low heat until translucent, about 10 minutes. Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute more.",
        "Add the chicken and cook for 5 to 7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until cooked through. Pour in the white wine and bring to a boil, scraping the bottom of the pan with a wooden spoon. Boil for 3 minutes, then add the crushed tomatoes, diced tomatoes, cannellini beans, chicken stock, chili powder, cumin, oregano, red pepper flakes, salt, and pepper. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat and simmer, covered, for at least 30 minutes for the flavors to blend.",
        "Serve hot with tortilla chips, grated cheddar, sour cream, and scallions."
